course: dictionary
lesson: 8762
title: Sever: cutting and cutting off
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Sever» is a verb, so it describes an action. It means to cut right through something so that it separates into parts: «The rope was severed by the sharp blade.» The verb changes its ending: sever, severs, severed, severing.
explain: Look at the clue words around it. In «The storm severed the power cable, and the town went dark», the word cable and the result, the town going dark, show that the cable was cut in two and could no longer carry electricity.
explain: The second meaning is about connections, which you cannot see or touch. «The country decided to sever links with its neighbour» means it ended all contact completely. The word links is the clue: links can be cut off just as ropes can.
explain: In «Heel pain in sport in children of about 8 to 14 is often Sever's disease», the capital S and the 's show that Sever is a name for a condition. It is not the verb, so always check the sentence before you decide what a word means.
fact: Sever is a verb: sever, severs, severed, severing.
fact: «Sever» means to cut right through something, separating it.
fact: «Sever» can also mean to end a connection completely, as in «sever ties».
fact: A severed wire can be dangerous, so never touch it: tell an adult straight away.
fact: A capital letter and 's can show that a word is a name, not an action word.
exercise: «The rope was severed by the sharp blade.» What does severed mean? | *Cut right through and separated | Tied tightly into a knot | Lost in the long grass | Painted a bright colour
exercise: Mia says the two countries will «sever links». What does sever links mean? | Share a new road together | *End the connection between them completely | Make a loud noise at the border | Build a bridge between them
exercise: Yesterday the storm ___ the power line. Which word fits the gap? | *severed | severs | sever | severing
test: «He decided to sever ties with his old team.» What does sever ties mean? | Join a new team | *End the connection completely | Practise more often | Ask for a bigger team
test: A sign says «Do not touch a severed wire.» Why? | It is shiny and new | It belongs to the school | *It could be dangerous | It has been painted red
exam: Which sentence uses sever to mean cut right through? | The dog sat quietly by the door | *The blade severed the cable cleanly | Ana felt happy all day | The children read the book for an hour
